This dataset contains identified Compound Hot-Dry-Windy events for 3108 counties across Contiguous United States.

Files in this dataset use the suffix _xxx to denote the severity level (occurrence rate related to a baseline period of 1980-1999) used to identify the events:

Suffix   Occurrence Rate
005        5 per thousand    
010       10 per thousand
050       50 per thousand

File Description
1. Spatial Reference
Filename: county.shapefile
Description: A geospatial vector file containing the boundaries of 3,108 counties in the CONUS.
Key Identifier: GEOID The unique code for each county. This serves as the primary index for linking data in the .npy and .csv files.

2. Event Dates
Filename: CHDW_Events_xxx.npy
Description: Contains the specific calendar dates where a CHDW event was identified for each county

3.Threshold Information
Filename: CHDW_Events_xxx.csv
Description: Contains the specific physical threshold values and percentile thresholds used to define the extreme events.
Columns:
ID : County unique identifier (GEOID)
Tem_percentile : Physical threshold value for air temperature, and daily actual value should EXCEED this value.
RH_percentile : Physical threshold value for relative humidity, and daily actual value should BE BELOW this value.
Wind_percentile : Physical threshold value for wind speed, and daily actual value should EXCEED this value.
Tem_threshold : Percentile threshold value for air temperature, and daily actual percentile should EXCEED this value.
RH_threshold : Percentile threshold value for relative humidity, and daily actual percentile should BE BELOW this value.
Wind_threshold : Percentile threshold value for wind speed, and daily actual percentile should EXCEED this value.

